---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Sessions and context"
  description="Local SQLite sessions, repository map, adaptive compaction, and durable async turns."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / SESSIONS</p>
    <h1>
      Keep the thread
      <br />
      <em>on your machine.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Sessions store messages and events in local SQLite. Context helpers help
      long work stay useful without inventing provider-native compaction APIs.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Local session store</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Create a session by choosing an existing workspace directory. The
          canonical path is stored with the session.
        </li>
        <li>
          State and creation events write in one transaction. SSE events use
          monotonic IDs so clients can resume from a cursor.
        </li>
        <li>
          Chat messages are capped at 1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes) of text. That is
          not Muse’s advertised token context window.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Repository map</h2>
      <p>
        An Aider-style extractive map ranks workspace files for context
        selection. In the TUI, run <code>/map</code>. HTTP:{" "}
        <code>GET /v1/sessions/&#123;id&#125;/workspace/map</code>.
        Capabilities: <code>workspace.repository_map</code> /{" "}
        <code>session.repository_map</code>. This is not a full semantic code
        index.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Adaptive compaction</h2>
      <p>
        When measured context grows large for an in-flight provider request,
        Veasel can compact extractively and emit a{" "}
        <code>session.compaction</code> event with measured bytes before/after.
        Optional summarizer:
      </p>
      <pre><code>VEASEL_SESSION_COMPACTION_SUMMARIZER=extractive   # default
VEASEL_SESSION_COMPACTION_SUMMARIZER=llm         # optional provider summary</code></pre>
      <p>
        LLM mode falls back on error, empty, or growth. Capability{" "}
        <code>session.compaction.summarizer</code> when enabled. Not
        provider-native compaction APIs; not invented cost. Details:{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/compatibility/session-compaction-summarizer.md">
          session-compaction-summarizer.md
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Durable async turns</h2>
      <p>
        Clients that send <code>Prefer: respond-async</code> get a durable
        operation ID. Queued turns resume after restart. If the process dies
        after a worker claimed the turn, startup marks it <code>uncertain</code>{" "}
        and never replays provider calls or tool effects. Inspect the workspace
        before retrying.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/api/`}>
        API and headless <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/troubleshooting/`}>
        Troubleshooting <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
